US-005 is done and the bead is closed. `scripts/check.sh` passed for `js-typecheck`, `js-lint`, `js-test` and `e2e` (the last two on separate runs). I did not run the Go steps. I did not do the playwright-cli browser check or take screenshots. The e2e spec runs at 390×844, but I did not try 1440×900.

- **New module:** `atlasLayerMap.ts` builds the map lazily. Until the page leaves `list`, nothing loads: no Leaflet, no data, no tiles. On the first change it reads the list's pages through the pager's own `fetchPosts`, so the filter matches the cards. It draws one marker per geotagged post. When the list changes, it adds and removes markers without rebuilding the map.
- **Wiring:** `GridPager` mounts the map and re-checks it on each re-arm. A new `filterKey` option, passed by `HomePage`, `TagPage` and `SearchPage`, tells the pager whether a re-arm means a different list.
- **Tests:** unit tests in `frontend/test/atlasLayerMap.test.ts` and a new e2e spec, `frontend/e2e/atlas-layer-map.test.ts`. The spec checks three things:
  - A tag page in `list` makes no Leaflet or tile requests.
  - `mapList` on that tag page shows exactly 2 markers, for the 2 geotagged posts, and tiles then load.
  - The home map shows at least 3 markers.
- **Profile pages:** there is no profile page in this tree, so that filter case has no code or test.
- **Page limit:** the map reads at most 30 pages per list, at the device-fit `per_page`. A very large list would need its own endpoint.
- **Flaky test:** the first full e2e run failed in `trustedTypes.test.ts` (a marker click was intercepted). It passed on rerun, and an earlier session logged other flaky failures in that file.

